Sheppard outlines several factors that correlate to deer movement. Temperature changes, wind speeds, and, cloud cover (lack thereof). Notably, moon phase does not reliably predict movement.  The dashboard is a visual representation of a mathematical model of these factors, augmented with Day-of-Week to account for general Monday-Friday hunting pressure, and a rut bonus factor. The final score is graded to show zero to five stars to let hunters know when the optimal time would be to go out. 
